{
  "note": "Gathering and crafting (roadmap item 44; core/game/game_craft.gd, checked by tools/check_data.gd). There is no recipe grid. An item is composed: the heir picks a form, a material they have gathered and up to three essences, and the result is the same kind of made item the loot generator builds (an id GameLoot.build reads), so what the player makes and what the world drops are one system. Materials come from hunts (the `drops` below, rolled on dice keyed on the seed, asked for by the screens only) and from salvaging gear (half the material back, and a gear's affixes become essences: a pelt keeps the wolf). An essence is an affix kept in a bottle. Stores belong to the family and pass down. Crafting needs a forge; salvaging can be done anywhere. A quality from 0 to 9 comes from the heir's level and Craft quality traits and a small keyed roll, and the item takes the world's grade, like a drop. Mythic items cannot be crafted.",
